# netsurf: iframes a script creates load -- cross-origin ones in a window
# and realm of their own, hidden ones included (patch 244; roadmap WS-B2)
# Generated 2026-10-11
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 243)
#
# The engine loaded only the iframes it parsed: iframe windows were made
# once, when the page became ready (browser_window_create_iframes, a fixed
# array of windows), so an iframe a script inserted got a box at most and
# never fetched -- hCaptcha's frames (claude.ai's email sign-in), OAuth
# widgets, embeds. Hidden iframes got no iframe record at all.
#
#  - desktop/browser_private.h, browser_window.c, frames.c: iframe windows
#    are allocated one by one (bw->iframes is an array of pointers), so it
#    can grow without moving a live window, and each remembers its
#    <iframe> element (iframe_node). Windows are re-linked to the rebuilt
#    box tree by that element, not by position (an iframe inserted before
#    the others shifted every window onto the wrong box); a window whose
#    element has no box now gets NULL (the scroll callback copes).
#    browser_window_recalculate_iframes notices an iframe record with no
#    window -- or a script having inserted an iframe -- and schedules
#    browser_window_sync_iframes, which makes windows for new CROSS-ORIGIN
#    frames (same-origin / blank script-made frames keep patch 143's
#    window in the page's realm: google's sign-in evaluates into it, and a
#    second load would run them twice), links their realm under the
#    frame's name or a page-unique "vbframe-N", and navigates them. A
#    frame with no box (display:none: hCaptcha's invisible checkbox frame)
#    is found in the DOM and gets a box-less 300x150 window. At most 8
#    script-made frame windows per page (each is a page and a realm).
#  - html/box_special.c: once the page is ready, a visibility:hidden
#    iframe is recorded too (hCaptcha's challenge frames); parsed hidden
#    frames stay skipped, as before. A late iframe record asks for the
#    window's notification (html_iframe_added_late); html/dom_event.c asks
#    when a script inserts an iframe (html_iframe_sync_wanted).
#  - html/html.c, browser_window.c: when an iframe window's page is DONE,
#    `load` fires at its element in the parent page (html_iframe_loaded) --
#    parsed iframes get it now too, as in browsers.
#  - vita/js_platform.c: a frame's document finds its own window while it
#    loads (window_with walks the iframe windows), so location.hash is the
#    frame's fragment (hCaptcha configures each frame from it).
#  - quickjs/macsurf_qjs.c + vita_polyfill.js: __vitaIframeKey(element)
#    answers the key its window was linked with (found by element, so a
#    box-less frame has one too), and iframe.contentWindow resolves it at
#    each send: a script reads contentWindow before the frame's window
#    exists. Also fixed: three content_get_type() calls on a struct
#    content * (the function takes an hlcache handle; an implicit
#    declaration hid it) -- the box-walk fallback of postMessage to a
#    child never matched.
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-xorigin-frame.html (+ -child) XFRAME 8/8
# (Chromium with the test CA: 8/8): a script-made frame from the gate's
# https port runs in its own realm and posts to its parent with its own
# origin, contentWindow.postMessage round trip, the iframe's load event,
# display:none and visibility:hidden frames load, and each reads its own
# fragment. Before this patch: 0/8 (nothing fetched).
#
# claude.ai/login: hCaptcha's four frames (two display:none checkbox,
# two visibility:hidden challenge) load and reach DONE, the challenge
# frames send challenge-loaded / get-url / site-setup to the page, which
# receives them with the right origin. hcaptcha.execute() still does not
# settle: the checkbox frames post nothing and the page sends nothing to
# any frame -- the next step is hCaptcha's own protocol (see the loop log).
#
# WIP (2026-10-11): NOT in the applied stack -- the Guardian regressed 74.1 -> 70.1 (visual 0.353 -> 0.267, top of page blank) once Sourcepoint's consent frame loads; making iframe canvases transparent (included here: redraw.c, browser_window.c) did not fix it. Gate with it: exit 0, XFRAME 8/8.
#
diff --git a/content/handlers/html/box_special.c b/content/handlers/html/box_special.c
